  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">221029_Start Fund ARC Replica (Drought Response Somalia)_WV_2023</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project is responding to the current food insecurity in the Baidoa and Burhabaka areas as a result of 5 consecutive failed rain seasons. Households are experiencing food insecurity with some communities projected to be facing IPC 5 (famine) between April and June 2023. The project therefore aims to support these communities through cash distributions. This is based on assessments which indicated that the market is active and operational and that the challenge is purchasing power for the affected persons. The project will distribute cash in 3 cycles from April to June 2023. The project is funded by the START Network Africa Risk Capacity (ARC) Programme payout</narrative>
  </description>
